RevizorInstructions
    Type: ApplicationKnowledge
    Role: AgentInstruction
    Purpose: AI agent instructions for Revizor — embedded in binary. Call trace_get_instructions at any time. No file access required.
    Version: 0.2

    StartupProtocol
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Critical protocol — always follow this order when starting a debugging session.

        Step1
            Type: Text
            Content: Call trace_ping FIRST. If pong — binary is alive, proceed. If connection refused — binary is not running. Stop. Do not call any other tools.

        Step2
            Type: Text
            Content: Call trace_get_instructions if you need the full reference. This document is always available through MCP.

        Step3
            Type: Text
            Content: Read logs via trace_search. session_id is optional. This is your primary debugging tool — no session creation required.

        Step4
            Type: Text
            Content: Before debugging new code — trace_audit to verify trace points exist. If missing — trace_inject with dry_run: true to preview, then without dry_run to apply.

        Step5
            Type: Text
            Content: After applying trace_inject — warn the user to clear __pycache__ and restart if the code runs in Docker or a virtual environment. Python may use old .pyc files and trace events will not appear.

        Step6
            Type: Text
            Content: Validate paths after adding — trace_validate_path on every new path. Format: [a-z0-9_.]+, max 120 chars, snake_case.

        Step7
            Type: Text
            Content: When done — trace_expire to clean up sessions. trace_shutdown for graceful process stop.

    CoreMethodology
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: The Golden Rule — the single most important concept in debugging with Revizor.

        GoldenRule
            Type: Text
            Content: Look for .enter without a matching .success — that is the breakage point. Every operation has an .enter at the start and a .success (or .failed) at the end. A missing .success means the operation did not finish — that is your bug.

    HowToReadTraceLogs
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Each entry is an event with path module.component.event.

        Pattern1
            Type: Text
            Caption: .enter → .success
            Content: Operation completed. Move on.

        Pattern2
            Type: Text
            Caption: .enter without .success
            Content: Operation did not finish. THIS IS THE BREAKAGE POINT.

        Pattern3
            Type: Text
            Caption: .enter → .failed
            Content: Operation threw an exception. Read data.reason for the error message.

        Pattern4
            Type: Text
            Caption: .decision
            Content: Branch point. Shows which condition was taken.

        Pattern5
            Type: Text
            Caption: Repeated .enter for same path
            Content: Loop or retry. Check the rate — may indicate a problem.

        Pattern6
            Type: Text
            Caption: .success with error field non-null
            Content: Partial success (best-effort). Operation completed but a sub-step failed — check the error.

    Recipes
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Ready-made debugging recipes for common scenarios.

        Recipe1
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Localize a crash in a known flow
            Content: Search by module name, look for .enter without .success.
            Command
                Type: Text
                Content: curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:9876/mcp -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"trace_search","arguments":{"search":"module_name.","lines":20}}}'

        Recipe2
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Verify a full end-to-end flow
            Content: Search for all entry points, count matching .success/.failed pairs.
            Command
                Type: Text
                Content: curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:9876/mcp -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"trace_search","arguments":{"search":".enter","path_filter":"module.*","lines":30}}}'

        Recipe3
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Three-layer audit
            Content: 1. trace_search — confirms WHAT happened and WHERE. 2. SQL — gives EXACT values. 3. Source code — explains WHY if the above two do not.

        Recipe4
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Before-and-after fix verification
            Content: Run the SAME trace_search before and after the fix. The difference is objective proof.

        Recipe5
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Precise data search
            Content: Events where field equals value, field exists, aggregate by path, or context around matches.
            Command
                Type: Text
                Content: trace_search '{"search":"","data_filter":"license_ok=false","lines":20}' — events where field equals value. trace_search '{"search":"","data_filter":"license_ok","lines":50}' — events where field exists. trace_search '{"search":"","data_filter":"license_ok=false","count_by":"path"}' — aggregate by path. trace_search '{"search":"order_id","context_lines":5,"lines":20}' — context around matches.

        Recipe6
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Compliance check before commit
            Content: Audit modules for trace import and validate all paths.

    BestPractices
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Eight rules for effective debugging with Revizor.

        Practice1
            Type: Text
            Content: Always ping before searching. trace_ping confirms the binary is alive.

        Practice2
            Type: Text
            Content: Search without session_id is your default. Sessions are only for time-range filtering (since/until).

        Practice3
            Type: Text
            Content: Search by module name as entry point. Do not guess the exact path — search broadly, then drill down.

        Practice4
            Type: Text
            Content: Combine trace_search + trace_read. Search finds the area, read gives full context.

        Practice5
            Type: Text
            Content: Compare before and after every fix. Same trace_search — difference is proof.

        Practice6
            Type: Text
            Content: Use trace_inject --dry-run for code verification. Shows file as unified diff.

        Practice7
            Type: Text
            Content: Use trace_audit before every commit. Checks compliance.

        Practice8
            Type: Text
            Content: Use trace_validate_path on every new path. No exceptions.

    PingFirstPattern
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Caption: Use this in scripts
        Content: Check if Revizor is alive before any operation.
        Command
            Type: Text
            Content: PING=$(curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:9876/mcp -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"trace_ping","arguments":{}}}'). If response contains pong — alive, proceed. Otherwise — start with /usr/local/bin/revizor serve.

    LargeDatabases
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: On databases with hundreds of thousands of events, trace_start may take tens of seconds. Use trace_search and trace_read without session_id for instant log access — sessions are not required for reading.

    GracefulShutdown
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Caption: To stop the Revizor process cleanly (flush buffers, close DB)
        Command
            Type: Text
            Content: curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:9876/mcp -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"trace_shutdown","arguments":{}}}'

    Tools
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Complete reference of all 35 MCP tools.

        Tool_trace_ping
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_ping
            Category: Diagnostic
            Purpose: Connectivity test with license status. Always call FIRST.

        Tool_trace_get_instructions
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_get_instructions
            Category: Diagnostic
            Purpose: Return this guide. Embedded in binary — no file access needed.

        Tool_trace_license_renew
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_license_renew
            Category: Diagnostic
            Purpose: Manual license renewal (replaces heartbeat).

        Tool_trace_read
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_read
            Category: LogReading
            Purpose: Read last N log lines. session_id optional.

        Tool_trace_search
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_search
            Category: LogReading
            Purpose: Full-text search with path_filter, data_filter, count_by, context_lines. PRIMARY TOOL.

        Tool_trace_config
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_config
            Category: LogReading
            Purpose: Show active trace points for a session.

        Tool_trace_tail
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_tail
            Category: LogReading
            Purpose: Streaming read — new events since last read (cursor-based).

        Tool_trace_start
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_start
            Category: Sessions
            Purpose: Create debug session and enable trace points by preset or path list.

        Tool_trace_enable
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_enable
            Category: Sessions
            Purpose: Enable a single point. Supports glob patterns (auth.**).

        Tool_trace_disable
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_disable
            Category: Sessions
            Purpose: Disable a single point.

        Tool_trace_expire
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_expire
            Category: Sessions
            Purpose: Force-expire a session — disable all points, set expiry to now.

        Tool_trace_kill
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_kill
            Category: Sessions
            Purpose: Kill one or all active sessions with cleanup.

        Tool_trace_validate_path
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_validate_path
            Category: Stats
            Purpose: Validate path format ([a-z0-9_.]+, max 120 chars).

        Tool_trace_why
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_why
            Category: Stats
            Purpose: Explain why a point is enabled/disabled — checks all glob rules.

        Tool_trace_list_sessions
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_list_sessions
            Category: Stats
            Purpose: List all active sessions.

        Tool_trace_presets_list
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_presets_list
            Category: Stats
            Purpose: List available presets (from DB, fallback to YAML).

        Tool_trace_preset_set
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_preset_set
            Category: Stats
            Purpose: Create or update a preset in the database. Supports ! excludes.

        Tool_trace_stats
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_stats
            Category: Stats
            Purpose: Session metrics — total events, unique paths, last event time.

        Tool_trace_list_points
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_list_points
            Category: Analysis
            Purpose: All known trace paths, grouped by module.

        Tool_trace_verify_coverage
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_verify_coverage
            Category: Analysis
            Purpose: Check chain integrity — each .enter must have .success/.failed.

        Tool_trace_diff
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_diff
            Category: Analysis
            Purpose: Compare two sessions — which trace paths differ.

        Tool_trace_cost
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_cost
            Category: Generation
            Purpose: Historical frequency of a trace point (events/minute).

        Tool_trace_generate_test
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_generate_test
            Category: Generation
            Purpose: Generate a pytest test from the event chain of a request_id.

        Tool_trace_suggest_coverage
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_suggest_coverage
            Category: Generation
            Purpose: Compare registered paths against expected .enter/.success/.failed pattern.

        Tool_trace_inject
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_inject
            Category: Instrumentation
            Purpose: Insert trace() calls into Python/TypeScript. dry_run, .bak.

        Tool_trace_remove
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_remove
            Category: Instrumentation
            Purpose: Remove trace() calls (reverse of trace_inject).

        Tool_trace_targets
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_targets
            Category: Instrumentation
            Purpose: Scan filesystem to prioritize files for injection (P1–P5).

        Tool_trace_audit
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_audit
            Category: Instrumentation
            Purpose: Audit modules for compliance. Use before commit.

        Tool_trace_session_summary
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_session_summary
            Category: Orchestrator
            Purpose: Session overview — events, unique paths, last event, status.

        Tool_trace_orchestrator_events
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_orchestrator_events
            Category: Orchestrator
            Purpose: Timeline of events for an orchestrator task (filter by task_id).

        Tool_trace_shutdown
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_shutdown
            Category: Process
            Purpose: Graceful stop — flush buffers, close DB, exit.

        Tool_trace_webhook_list
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_webhook_list
            Category: Webhook
            Purpose: List registered webhooks and delivery status.

        Tool_trace_webhook_test
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_webhook_test
            Category: Webhook
            Purpose: Test ping to a specific webhook.

        Tool_trace_update_check
            Type: Card
            Role: ToolReference
            Id: trace_update_check
            Category: Diagnostic
            Purpose: Check for Revizor updates (manual + automatic at startup).

    SDK
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: How users send trace events — via SDK or trace_inject.

        Python
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Python SDK
            Command
                Type: Text
                Content: from revizor_sdk import configure, trace, trace_start
                Content: configure(endpoint="http://localhost:9876")
                Content: trace("my_module.my_function.enter", {"key": "value"})
                Content: end = trace_start("my_module.operation") ... end({"result": "ok"})

        TypeScript
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: TypeScript SDK
            Command
                Type: Text
                Content: import { initTrace, trace, traceStart } from '@ais-platform/revizor-sdk'
                Content: initTrace({ apiBaseUrl: 'http://localhost:9876' })
                Content: trace('my_module.my_function.enter', { key: 'value' })
                Content: const end = traceStart('my_module.operation') ... end({ result: 'ok' })

        SDKBehavior
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: SDK behavior
            Text
                Content: Fire-and-forget — trace() never waits for server response
            Text
                Content: Never-throw — exceptions are swallowed, your app never crashes because of tracing
            Text
                Content: Zero-overhead when disabled — if a point is off, trace() returns instantly
            Text
                Content: Client-side sanitization — passwords, tokens, emails are masked before sending
            Text
                Content: Batching — events are queued and sent in batches (every 100ms or 50 events)

            DisableSDK
                Type: Section
                Role: AgentInstruction
                Caption: Disable SDK to prevent console noise
                Content: TypeScript — initTrace({ apiBaseUrl: '' }) disables all tracing. Python — configure(enabled=False). Always disable in environments where Revizor is not running.

    TraceInject
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: trace_inject — automatic insertion of trace() calls. Dry-run first, then apply.

        Text
            Content: trace_inject adds import trace, inserts .enter at function start, .success before each return, .failed before each raise/throw. Module name auto-detected from path. Language auto-detected from extension. Always preview with dry_run: true first.

        PythonSpecifics
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Content: One-liner functions (def f(x): return expr) are automatically split into multi-line. Nested functions, class methods, and async functions supported.

        TypeScriptSpecifics
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Content: PascalCase component names are auto-converted to snake_case in trace paths. export function NavMenu() → trace path nav_menu.enter.

        AfterApply
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: After applying trace_inject
            Content: If the injected code runs in Docker or a virtual environment — clear Python bytecode cache (__pycache__ directories and .pyc files) and restart the process. Python may continue using old bytecode, making trace events invisible. The binary warns about this after each successful inject.

    TraceRemove
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: trace_remove — reverse of trace_inject. Removes all previously injected trace() calls. Always preview with dry_run: true first.

    Presets
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Presets are ready-made sets of trace paths for common debugging scenarios. List with trace_presets_list, pass preset name to trace_start.

    Streaming
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: trace_tail streams new events as they arrive. Cursor-based — first call returns last N events, subsequent calls return new events since last call.

    SessionComparison
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: trace_diff compares two debugging sessions. Useful after a fix — session A = broken run, session B = fixed run.

    TestGeneration
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: trace_generate_test generates a pytest test from a real request's event chain. Pass request_id from trace events.

    OrchestratorEvents
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: trace_orchestrator_events shows timeline of events for an orchestrator task. Filter by task_id.

    Webhooks
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Revizor can notify external systems when specific trace events occur. Configure in revizor.yaml. Delivery is async with 3 retries at 5-second intervals.

    Updates
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: trace_update_check — manual check for Revizor updates. Binary also checks automatically at startup.

    AccessMethods
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: Four ways to access Revizor tools.

        Method1
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: MCP Direct (Claude Code, Gemini, Cursor)
            Content: Binary registered in MCP host config — exposes tools natively.

        Method2
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: HTTP JSON-RPC (curl, scripts, CI/CD)
            Content: Binary runs as revizor serve on port 9876. All 35 tools via POST /mcp. Most universal method.

        Method3
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: CLI Wrapper (AI agents WITHOUT tool_calls — DeepSeek, local models)
            Content: python3 modules/mcp_client_cli_0_1_0/mcp_client_cli_0_1_0.py --server './revizor --mcp' --tool trace_search --args '{"search":"elevation","lines":50}'. Only works with --mcp (stdio) mode, NOT revizor serve.

        Method4
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Prompt Adapter (LLMs without ANY tool/function calling)
            Content: For models that cannot call tools at all. Adapter converts Revizor tools into text instructions. LLM outputs <revizor><tool>trace_ping</tool></revizor> — adapter executes and injects result back. Least efficient, last resort.

    Docker
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: If application runs in Docker but Revizor is on host — bind to 0.0.0.0 in revizor.yaml, pass REVIZOR_URL=http://host.docker.internal:9876 to container, create session at startup and pass REVIZOR_SESSION_ID.

    Licensing
        Type: Section
        Role: AgentInstruction
        Purpose: License tiers, limits, and troubleshooting.

        TierComparison
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Tier Comparison

            Community
                Type: Card
                Role: PricingCard
                Caption: Community (no key)
                Sessions: 1
                EventsPerDay: 100
                Machines: 1
                Tools: Basic (3)
                Storage: SQLite

            Trial
                Type: Card
                Role: PricingCard
                Caption: Trial
                Sessions: unlimited
                EventsPerDay: unlimited
                Machines: 3
                Tools: Full
                Storage: SQLite

            Indie
                Type: Card
                Role: PricingCard
                Caption: Indie
                Sessions: 5
                EventsPerDay: 10,000
                Machines: 3
                Tools: Full
                Storage: SQLite

            Pro
                Type: Card
                Role: PricingCard
                Caption: Pro
                Sessions: 10
                EventsPerDay: 100,000
                Machines: 10
                Tools: Full
                Storage: PostgreSQL

            Enterprise
                Type: Card
                Role: PricingCard
                Caption: Enterprise
                Sessions: unlimited
                EventsPerDay: unlimited
                Machines: unlimited
                Tools: Full
                Storage: PostgreSQL

            Privileged
                Type: Card
                Role: PricingCard
                Caption: Privileged
                Sessions: unlimited
                EventsPerDay: unlimited
                Machines: Custom
                Tools: Full
                Storage: PostgreSQL

        KeyRules
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: Key Rules

            Rule
                Type: Text
                Content: Sunday Unlimited — all tiers get unlimited usage every Sunday (no session/event limits).

            Rule
                Type: Text
                Content: Community mode activates automatically when no license key is provided or the key is invalid.

            Rule
                Type: Text
                Content: PostgreSQL requires postgres feature in the license key + storage.type: postgres in revizor.yaml.

            Rule
                Type: Text
                Content: Max Version — perpetual licenses (exp=-1) may have max_ver. Binary version must not exceed it.

            Rule
                Type: Text
                Content: Activation — first launch with a license key registers the machine. trace_license_renew sends heartbeats.

            Rule
                Type: Text
                Content: Enterprise offline — Enterprise licenses work without activation or heartbeats.

        Troubleshooting
            Type: Section
            Role: AgentInstruction
            Caption: When the user hits a limit

            Symptom1
                Type: Text
                Caption: trace_start fails
                Content: Too many active sessions. Fix — trace_kill old sessions, or upgrade tier.

            Symptom2
                Type: Text
                Caption: Events not appearing
                Content: Daily event limit reached. Fix — wait until next day (or Sunday), or upgrade tier.

            Symptom3
                Type: Text
                Caption: Tools return errors
                Content: Community mode (3 tools only). Fix — provide a license key.
